# Cursor AI Rules for AI Agent Study Guide

## Project Type
Documentation repository - no implementation code.

## Context
This repo documents OpenAI Codex-RS architecture to teach AI agent development patterns.

## Key Files to Reference
- docs/architecture-diagram.md - Mermaid diagrams (primary source of truth)
- docs/codex-architecture.html - Interactive HTML diagrams
- llms-full.txt - Complete context

## Documentation Standards

### Diagrams
- Use Mermaid syntax
- Include source file links to GitHub
- Validate against actual Codex-RS code

### Writing Style
- Concise, no filler
- Use tables for mappings
- Include Rust code snippets
- Explicit over implicit

## Architecture Facts

### Critical Understanding
TUI → ThreadManager (direct)
NOT: TUI → MessageProcessor → ThreadManager

MessageProcessor is ONLY for external JSON-RPC clients.

### Key Types
- Op: UserTurn, ExecApproval, Interrupt, Undo
- EventMsg: TurnStarted, TurnComplete, ExecApprovalRequest, AgentMessage
- Event: { id: String, msg: EventMsg }

## Do Not
- Create implementation code
- Add build dependencies
- Modify diagrams without source verification
